This repository intentionally keeps only the Debian packaging recipe.

The intended unpack/import step is handled by `gbp import-orig`, using the
configuration in `debian/gbp.conf`.

Typical flow:

  cd /root/uboot/linux_recipe
  git fetch origin latest upstream/latest pristine-tar --tags || true
  git worktree add ../linux-build origin/master
  cd ../linux-build
  version=$(dpkg-parsechangelog --show-field Version | sed 's/-[^-]*$//')
  uscan --check-dirname-level 0 --download-current-version --rename --destdir ..
  gbp import-orig --no-interactive --debian-branch=latest \
    --upstream-branch=upstream/latest --upstream-version "$version" \
    ../linux-cv181x-sodoport_${version}.orig.tar.xz

Build a source package:

  dpkg-source -b .

Build a binary package:

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b -a riscv64

Patches are stored in `debian/patches` because the source format is
`3.0 (quilt)`. Never edit those patch files by hand and do not generate them
with `dpkg-source --commit` or `quilt refresh`.

Make kernel changes in a clean Git checkout of the imported upstream source.
Apply the existing patch series as commits, edit the source, and commit each
logical change. Export each resulting commit with:

  git format-patch -1 --stdout > /path/to/debian/patches/NNNN-description.patch

Add the generated patch filename to `debian/patches/series`, then verify the
complete series from a clean source tree with `dpkg-source -b .`.

The initial board config and DTS patch were seeded from the local
`/root/uboot/sg2002` Alpine package draft and translated into Debian package
inputs.

The resulting binary packages follow Debian's normal kernel split:

  linux-image-7.1.0-cv181x-sodoport
    versioned kernel image package with /boot artifacts, modules, and DTBs
  linux-image-cv181x-sodoport
    unversioned meta-package for the current kernel
  linux-source-cv181x-sodoport
    patched source bundle under /usr/src

The checked-in `debian/config/cv181x-sodoport.config` is only a temporary
generated seed. The intended long-term source of truth is:

  debian/config/base/milkv-duo_defconfig
  debian/config/fragments/debian-common.fragment
  debian/config/fragments/*.fragment

You can regenerate the board config from those inputs with:

  debian/scripts/update-config.sh /path/to/linux
